Report a directory that rm -r cannot open.
When opendir() failed, as for a directory without read permission, or
on Windows one whose path is too long to list, remove_file() returned
failure without a message. rm -r then left the directory and exited
with status 1 without saying why. Use warn_opendir() so that the
failure is reported like the others.

---
 libbb/remove_file.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libbb/remove_file.c
+++ b/libbb/remove_file.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 				return 0;
 		}
 
-		dp = opendir(path);
+		dp = warn_opendir(path);
 		if (dp == NULL) {
 			return -1;
 		}
